<file path="docs/design/EDD-001-Orchestrator-v2.md">
  1: # EDD-001 — Orchestrator v2
  2: 
  3: **Status:** Draft
  4: 
  5: **Owner:** Human OS
  6: 
  7: **Related Documents:**
  8: 
  9: - HUMAN_OS_ARCHITECTURE_V1.md
 10: - ADR-001-Orchestrator.md
 11: 
 12: ---
 13: 
 14: # 1. Overview
 15: 
 16: This document describes the implementation plan for evolving the Human OS orchestrator into the central coordination layer of the platform.
 17: 
 18: The orchestrator already coordinates several capabilities, including intent detection, skill routing, context construction, and AI invocation.
 19: 
 20: The goal of Orchestrator v2 is to integrate additional platform capabilities while preserving existing behavior.
 21: 
 22: ---
 23: 
 24: # 2. Problem Statement
 25: 
 26: Today the orchestrator coordinates:
 27: 
 28: - Brain initialization
 29: - Intent detection
 30: - Skill routing
 31: - Context building
 32: - AI provider
 33: 
 34: However, Human OS now contains additional capabilities that are not yet integrated:
 35: 
 36: - Digital DNA
 37: - Profile Engine
 38: - Profile Enrichment Engine
 39: 
 40: As a result, the AI does not yet benefit from long-term knowledge about the user.
 41: 
 42: ---
 43: 
 44: # 3. Goals
 45: 
 46: The objectives of Orchestrator v2 are:
 47: 
 48: - Integrate the Human Profile into the orchestration pipeline.
 49: - Execute the Enrichment Engine during conversation.
 50: - Preserve existing runtime behavior.
 51: - Prepare the orchestrator for future Memory integration.
 52: - Maintain a single orchestration layer.
 53: 
 54: ---
 55: 
 56: # 4. Non-Goals
 57: 
 58: This milestone does NOT include:
 59: 
 60: - Memory persistence
 61: - Planner integration
 62: - UI changes
 63: - Dashboard updates
 64: - Voice support
 65: - Multi-agent orchestration
 66: 
 67: These capabilities will be introduced in future milestones.
 68: 
 69: ---
 70: 
 71: # 5. Current Request Flow
 72: 
 73: User
 74: 
 75: ↓
 76: 
 77: Initialize Brain
 78: 
 79: ↓
 80: 
 81: Extract Memory
 82: 
 83: ↓
 84: 
 85: Detect Intent
 86: 
 87: ↓
 88: 
 89: Execute Skills
 90: 
 91: ↓
 92: 
 93: Build Context
 94: 
 95: ↓
 96: 
 97: AI Service
 98: 
 99: ↓
100: 
101: Response
102: 
103: ---
104: 
105: # 6. Target Request Flow
106: 
107: User
108: 
109: ↓
110: 
111: Initialize Brain
112: 
113: ↓
114: 
115: Load Human Profile
116: 
117: ↓
118: 
119: Run Enrichment Engine
120: 
121: ↓
122: 
123: Extract Memory
124: 
125: ↓
126: 
127: Detect Intent
128: 
129: ↓
130: 
131: Execute Skills
132: 
133: ↓
134: 
135: Build Context
136: 
137: ↓
138: 
139: AI Service
140: 
141: ↓
142: 
143: Profile Update (Future)
144: 
145: ↓
146: 
147: Memory Update (Future)
148: 
149: ↓
150: 
151: Response
152: 
153: ---
154: 
155: # 7. Implementation Plan
156: 
157: Phase 1
158: 
159: - Load Human Profile.
160: - Execute Enrichment Engine.
161: - Preserve existing behavior.
162: 
163: Phase 2
164: 
165: - Inject Human Profile into the Context Builder.
166: 
167: Phase 3
168: 
169: - Allow AI responses to update the profile.
170: 
171: Phase 4
172: 
173: - Introduce Memory integration.
174: 
175: ---
176: 
177: # 8. Risks
178: 
179: Potential risks include:
180: 
181: - Changing request order.
182: - Breaking skill routing.
183: - Increasing orchestration complexity.
184: - Tight coupling between modules.
185: 
186: These risks will be mitigated through incremental implementation and behavior-preserving refactoring.
187: 
188: ---
189: 
190: # 9. Success Criteria
191: 
192: The milestone is considered complete when:
193: 
194: - Existing behavior remains unchanged.
195: - Human Profile is available to the orchestrator.
196: - Enrichment Engine executes successfully.
197: - All tests continue to pass.
198: - The architecture remains modular.
199: 
200: ---
201: 
202: # 10. Future Work
203: 
204: Future milestones will extend the orchestrator with:
205: 
206: - Long-term Memory
207: - Planner
208: - Calendar
209: - Email
210: - GitHub
211: - Voice
212: - Vision
213: - Multi-agent coordination
214: 
215: Orchestrator v2 provides the architectural foundation for these capabilities.
</file>

